<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Output Alignment</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a given student input sequence <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and its equivalent teacher input sequence <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, we first extract hidden representation using the student model <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and the frozen teacher model <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, in sequence and obtain <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{X}_{s}=F_{s}(X_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{X}_{s}=F_{s}(X_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{X}_{t}=F_{t}(X_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{X}_{t}=F_{t}(X_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. We utilize a non-linear mapping, defined by the operators, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{F}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{F}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{F}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{F}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math>, for encoding the hidden representations, obtaining <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{h^{{}^{\prime}}}^{X}_{s}=\tilde{F}_{s}(h^{X}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>h</mi><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{h^{{}^{\prime}}}^{X}_{s}=\tilde{F}_{s}(h^{X}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{h^{{}^{\prime}}}^{X}_{ts}=\tilde{F}_{ts}(h^{X}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>h</mi><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{h^{{}^{\prime}}}^{X}_{ts}=\tilde{F}_{ts}(h^{X}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. For each task <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\in\mathbb{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝕋</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\in\mathbb{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use task-specific linear layers for both <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TS Aligner</span> and the student to obtain the outputs, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\mathcal{T}}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\mathcal{T}}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\mathcal{T}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\mathcal{T}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively. We use the task-specific loss function <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L_{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L_{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">e.g.,</span> cross-entropy for classification and mean squared error for regression) to compute loss against the ground-truth <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> on the training dataset. For <span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TS Aligner</span>, the output loss is given as,</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{(1)}_{ts}=\mathcal{L_{T}}(Y^{\mathcal{T}},o^{\mathcal{T}}_{ts})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{(1)}_{ts}=\mathcal{L_{T}}(Y^{\mathcal{T}},o^{\mathcal{T}}_{ts}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For the student model, the output loss is computed as the weighted sum of the loss against the ground-truth and the logit matching loss <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hinton et al., 2015</a>)</cite> with the aligner as,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{(1)}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{(1)}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)\cdot\mathcal{L_{T}}(Y^{\mathcal{T}},o^{\mathcal{T}}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\alpha)\cdot\mathcal{L_{T}}(Y^{\mathcal{T}},o^{\mathcal{T}}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\alpha\Big\|\Phi\Bigl(\frac{o^{\mathcal{T}}_{ts}}{\tau}\Bigr)-\Phi\Bigl(\frac{o^{\mathcal{T}}_{s}}{\tau}\Bigr)\Big\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\alpha\Big\|\Phi\Bigl(\frac{o^{\mathcal{T}}_{ts}}{\tau}\Bigr)-\Phi\Bigl(\frac{o^{\mathcal{T}}_{s}}{\tau}\Bigr)\Big\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For the classification task, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> is the softmax function, whereas it is an identity function for the regression task. <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> are the hyperparameters representing the output loss and temperature factors, respectively. We use <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> as default.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Manifold Alignment</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al. (2019)</a></cite> suggested an additional loss between the teacher and student hidden representations to enforce the student model in learning the feature representations similar to the teacher. However, minimizing the point-wise distance between the teacher and student representations can distort the information learned in the student’s original modality in cross-modal distillation. Therefore, we first project the representations obtained from <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TS Aligner</span> and the student models to a shared manifold and subsequently minimize their distance on the common subspace. We use two orthogonal projection mapping, <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, to project the original teacher and student hidden representations to a common subspace to obtain <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{ts}({h^{{}^{\prime}}}^{X}_{ts})=p^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>h</mi><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ts}({h^{{}^{\prime}}}^{X}_{ts})=p^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P_{s}({h^{{}^{\prime}}}^{X}_{s})=p^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>h</mi><mrow></mrow><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></mmultiscripts><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{s}({h^{{}^{\prime}}}^{X}_{s})=p^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> belong to the same dimensional subspace, therefore the manifold equivalence can be enforced with traditional similarity or distance measures. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huo et al. (2021)</a></cite>, we propose an inner-product-based distance measure,</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{cosine}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=1-\langle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{ts},\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{s}\rangle" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{cosine}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=1-\langle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{ts},\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{s}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where, <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle.,.\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle.,.\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the inner product between two vectors, and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{cosine}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{cosine}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the semantic similarity between teacher and student manifolds. Similarly, we formulate two other losses, <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{euclid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{euclid}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}</annotation></semantics></math>, to measure the distance between two manifolds in Euclidean space.</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{euclid}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=\Big\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{ts}-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{s}\Big\|_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{euclid}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=\Big\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{ts}-\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{s}\Big\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}||p^{x_{i}}_{ts}-p^{x_{i}}_{s}||_{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}||p^{x_{i}}_{ts}-p^{x_{i}}_{s}||_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{euclid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{euclid}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute Euclidean distance between the centroid of the teacher and student projection vectors, whereas, with <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute the expected pairwise (element-wise) distances between the teacher and student projection vectors. Different loss formulations induce different student model regularizations, encouraging the student to learn different cross-modal abstractions. For the rest of the paper, we generalize these three losses as <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{manifold}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{manifold}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1.</span> <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}</annotation></semantics></math> enforces highest regularization effect than <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{euclid}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{euclid}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{cosine}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{cosine}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> We would like to show that <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})\geq\mathcal{L}_{euclid}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})&gt;||\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}||\cdot||\overline{p^{X}_{s}}||\cdot\sqrt{\mathcal{L}_{cosine}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})\geq\mathcal{L}_{euclid}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})&gt;||\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}||\cdot||\overline{p^{X}_{s}}||\cdot\sqrt{\mathcal{L}_{cosine}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})}</annotation></semantics></math>. From Equation <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.2 Manifold Alignment ‣ 3 Proposed Methodology ‣ From Images to Words: Efficient Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation to Language Models from Black-box Teachers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> we obtain,</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{euclid}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=\Big\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(p^{x_{i}}_{ts}-p^{x_{i}}_{s})\Big\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{euclid}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=\Big\|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(p^{x_{i}}_{ts}-p^{x_{i}}_{s})\Big\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Big\|p^{x_{i}}_{ts}-p^{x_{i}}_{s}\Big\|_{2}\text{(Triangle inequality)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>(Triangle inequality)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Big\|p^{x_{i}}_{ts}-p^{x_{i}}_{s}\Big\|_{2}\text{(Triangle inequality)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{L}_{elementwise}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We denote <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}p^{x_{i}}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{p^{X}_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{p^{X}_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then from Equations <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2 Manifold Alignment ‣ 3 Proposed Methodology ‣ From Images to Words: Efficient Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation to Language Models from Black-box Teachers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> and  <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.2 Manifold Alignment ‣ 3 Proposed Methodology ‣ From Images to Words: Efficient Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation to Language Models from Black-box Teachers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we obtain,</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{euclid}^{2}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}-\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|^{2}_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{euclid}^{2}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})=\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}-\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|^{2}_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|^{2}_{2}+\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|^{2}_{2}-2\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}&lt;\overline{p^{X}_{ts}},\overline{p^{X}_{s}}&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|^{2}_{2}+\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|^{2}_{2}-2\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}&lt;\overline{p^{X}_{ts}},\overline{p^{X}_{s}}&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S3.Ex7.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">From AM-GM inequality</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq 2\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}-2\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}&lt;\overline{p^{X}_{ts}},\overline{p^{X}_{s}}&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq 2\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}-2\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}&lt;\overline{p^{X}_{ts}},\overline{p^{X}_{s}}&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}\mathcal{L}_{cosine}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}\mathcal{L}_{cosine}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&gt;\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}\mathcal{L}_{cosine}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&gt;\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{ts}}\Big\|_{2}\Big\|\overline{p^{X}_{s}}\Big\|_{2}\mathcal{L}_{cosine}(p^{X}_{ts},p^{X}_{s}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Auxiliary Output Alignment</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further regularize the student representations, we incorporate an auxiliary output head on <span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TS Aligner</span> and student projection heads. We align the models to learn appropriate manifold projections that maximize their performance on downstream tasks by incorporating an auxiliary output head on both teacher and student projection vectors. Given the auxiliary output <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\mathcal{T}}_{aux_{ts}}=O^{\mathcal{T}}_{aux_{ts}}(p^{X}_{ts})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\mathcal{T}}_{aux_{ts}}=O^{\mathcal{T}}_{aux_{ts}}(p^{X}_{ts})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{\mathcal{T}}_{aux_{s}}=O^{\mathcal{T}}_{aux_{s}}(p^{X}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{\mathcal{T}}_{aux_{s}}=O^{\mathcal{T}}_{aux_{s}}(p^{X}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math>, we calculate the auxiliary losses, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{(2)}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{(2)}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}^{(2)}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}^{(2)}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, similar to Equations <a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3.1 Output Alignment ‣ 3 Proposed Methodology ‣ From Images to Words: Efficient Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation to Language Models from Black-box Teachers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.1 Output Alignment ‣ 3 Proposed Methodology ‣ From Images to Words: Efficient Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation to Language Models from Black-box Teachers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. We establish homeomorphism between topological spaces to understand how the intertwining of different alignments ensure the effectiveness of multimodal knowledge transfer.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1.</span> A function <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\rightarrow Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\rightarrow Y</annotation></semantics></math> is called <span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">homeomorphism</span> if <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is bijective (<span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.,</span> one-to-one and onto) and continuous, and the inverse function <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> exists and is continuous too.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.</span> Two topological spaces, <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>, are called <span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">homeomorphic</span> if a homeomorphism exists between them. Homeomorphism ensures that two spaces are topologically similar and exhibit structural equivalence.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2.</span> Let’s assume a sequence of inputs <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and their corresponding aligner projection space <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math>, student projection space <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, teacher output space <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and student output space <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, auxiliary teacher output space <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{aux_{ts}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{aux_{ts}}</annotation></semantics></math> and auxiliary student output space <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{aux_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{aux_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> are homeomorphic, <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> are also homeomorphic. Similarly, <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{aux_{ts}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{aux_{ts}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{aux_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{aux_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> are also homeomorphic.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.10877v1/commutative_diagram.png" id="S3.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:480/270;" width="480" height="270" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Commutative diagram between the manifold, output and auxiliary output spaces. The bold lines denote the functions already defined between the spaces. The dashed lines indicate the functions we want to establish in the proof of Proposition 2.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof.</span> If <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> are homeomorphic, then there exists a continuous bijective function <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:p^{X}_{ts}\rightarrow p^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:p^{X}_{ts}\rightarrow p^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that the inverse <math id="S3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{-1}:p^{X}_{s}\rightarrow p^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{-1}:p^{X}_{s}\rightarrow p^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> is also continuous. Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.3 Auxiliary Output Alignment ‣ 3 Proposed Methodology ‣ From Images to Words: Efficient Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation to Language Models from Black-box Teachers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> highlights the mapping between different spaces.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Being an orthogonal projection matrix, <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> has its inverse <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P^{T}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P^{T}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, the inverse of <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> exists. Being linear maps, all the functions <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ts},P_{s},O_{ts},O_{s},O_{aux_{ts}}\text{ and }O_{aux_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ts},P_{s},O_{ts},O_{s},O_{aux_{ts}}\text{ and }O_{aux_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math> are continuous. To prove that the output spaces <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> are homeomorphic, we need to establish two continuous bijection functions <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(1)}:o^{X}_{ts}\rightarrow o^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(1)}:o^{X}_{ts}\rightarrow o^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(2)}:o^{X}_{s}\rightarrow o^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(2)}:o^{X}_{s}\rightarrow o^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}=g^{(2)}\circ g^{(1)}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}=g^{(2)}\circ g^{(1)}=I</annotation></semantics></math>. Being finite spaces with the same cardinality (same as the batch size), the surjectivity of functions <math id="S3.SS3.p6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{ts},P_{s},O_{ts},O_{s},O_{aux_{ts}}\text{ and }O_{aux_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{ts},P_{s},O_{ts},O_{s},O_{aux_{ts}}\text{ and }O_{aux_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>, suggests injectivity of these functions. Therefore, all these functions are bijections.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(1)}\circ O_{ts}\circ{P_{ts}}^{-1}=O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}\circ f." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(1)}\circ O_{ts}\circ{P_{ts}}^{-1}=O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}\circ f.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, for a given point <math id="S3.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{x}_{s}\in P_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{x}_{s}\in P_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g^{(2)}\circ O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}=O_{ts}\circ{P_{ts}}^{-1}\circ f^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g^{(2)}\circ O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}=O_{ts}\circ{P_{ts}}^{-1}\circ f^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}\circ O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}=g^{(1)}\circ O_{ts}\circ{P_{ts}}^{-1}\circ f^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}\circ O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}=g^{(1)}\circ O_{ts}\circ{P_{ts}}^{-1}\circ f^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}\circ O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}=O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}\circ f\circ f^{-1}(\text{Eq~\ref{eq:proof2_eq1}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Eq </mtext><mtext><a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.3 Auxiliary Output Alignment ‣ 3 Proposed Methodology ‣ From Images to Words: Efficient Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation to Language Models from Black-box Teachers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}\circ O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}=O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}\circ f\circ f^{-1}(\text{Eq~\ref{eq:proof2_eq1}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}\circ O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}=O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}\circ O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}=O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The function <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> has a right inverse due to its surjectivity. Similarly, <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> also has a right inverse. Therefore, we get <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(1)}\circ g^{(2)}=I</annotation></semantics></math>. A similar formulation leads us to <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(2)}\circ g^{(1)}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(2)}\circ g^{(1)}=I</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, we can simplify</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(1)}=O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}\circ f\circ P_{ts}\circ O^{-1}_{ts}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>P</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msubsup><mi>O</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(1)}=O_{s}\circ{P_{s}}^{-1}\circ f\circ P_{ts}\circ O^{-1}_{ts}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p">As a composition of continuous bijections, <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is also a continuous bijection. Therefore, <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(1)}</annotation></semantics></math> is a homeomorphism. A similar formulation can be used to establish that <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(1)}_{aux}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(1)}_{aux}</annotation></semantics></math> is a homeomorphism. Therefore, a homeomorphic relationship between <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> ensures homeomorphic relationship between <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{ts}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{ts}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and homeomorphic relationship between <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{aux_{ts}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{aux_{ts}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o^{X}_{aux_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mi>X</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o^{X}_{aux_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition 2 suggests how an equivalence between the teacher and student manifolds can establish equivalence between their associated output and auxiliary output spaces. Therefore, we can regularize the student by minimizing the distance from the teacher manifold. As opposed to vokenization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tan and Bansal, 2020</a>)</cite> and VidLanKD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, which use pre-training objectives to train the teacher models, we optimize <span id="S3.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TS Aligner</span> on task-specific objectives, allowing task-specific knowledge diffusion to students. The final <span id="S3.SS3.p13.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TS Aligner</span> loss is calculated as <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{t}=\mathcal{L}^{(1)}_{ts}+\gamma\mathcal{L}^{(2)}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{t}=\mathcal{L}^{(1)}_{ts}+\gamma\mathcal{L}^{(2)}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the student model, we use the output loss, auxiliary output loss, and manifold alignment loss to calculate the final training loss as <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{s}=\mathcal{L}^{(1)}_{s}+\gamma\mathcal{L}^{(2)}_{s}+\beta\mathcal{L}_{manifold}(p^{X}_{t},p^{X}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>X</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{s}=\mathcal{L}^{(1)}_{s}+\gamma\mathcal{L}^{(2)}_{s}+\beta\mathcal{L}_{manifold}(p^{X}_{t},p^{X}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="S3.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> are hyperparameters used to assign weightage to the manifold and auxiliary output alignment loss, respectively. We use <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1</annotation></semantics></math> by default.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experimental Setup</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tasks.</span> We apply <span id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ARMADA</span> on <span id="S4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">seven</span> student LMs and <span id="S4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">four</span> multimodal teacher models and compare it against ten unimodal and three multimodal KD methods across 12 NLU tasks and <span id="S4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5</span> instruction-following tasks. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2022)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al. (2021)</a></cite>, we consider four different NLU tasks from SuperGLUE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2019</a>)</cite> – CB, COPA, BoolQ and WiC, and eight tasks from GLUE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2018</a>)</cite> – CoLA, MRPC, RTE, STS-B (categorized as <span id="S4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GLUE-small</span>), SST-2, MNLI, QNLI and QQP (categorized as <span id="S4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">GLUE-large</span>). We also consider Multimodal-IMDb <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arevalo et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, a classification task to predict movie genres based on poster images (image modality) and additional metadata, including plot summaries (text modality), etc. Additionally, we consider five commonsense reasoning tasks – HellaSwag <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib80" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zellers et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, WinoGrande <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib81" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sakaguchi et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, ARC-easy, ARC-challenge <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">Clark et al., 2018</a>)</cite> and OpenBookQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib83" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mihaylov et al., 2018</a>)</cite> and three mathematical reasoning tasks – MultiArith <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">Roy and Roth, 2016</a>)</cite>, SingleEq <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib85" title="" class="ltx_ref">Koncel-Kedziorski et al., 2016</a>)</cite> and AQuA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib86" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ling et al., 2017</a>)</cite>. <span id="S4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For instruction-following experiments, we fine-tune the student models on Dolly-15K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al. (2024)</a></cite> dataset and evaluate on Dolly, SelfInst <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2022a)</a></cite>, Vicuna <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chiang et al. (2023)</a></cite>, SNI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2022b)</a></cite> and UNI <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Honovich et al. (2023)</a></cite> datasets.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Student and teacher models.</span> We consider <span id="S4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">seven</span> different pre-trained language models, including BERT-base <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Devlin et al., 2018</a>)</cite> (<math id="S4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="111M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">111M</annotation></semantics></math> parameters), pre-trained BERT 6-layer (<math id="S4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="66M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>66</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">66M</annotation></semantics></math> parameters), DeBERTa-v2-xxlarge <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">He et al., 2020</a>)</cite> (<math id="S4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.4B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1.4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.4B</annotation></semantics></math> parameters), OPT-1.3B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, LLaMA-7B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, LLaMA-3.1-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubey et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and LLaMA-3.2-3B<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
          The pre-trained models are obtained from <a href="https://huggingface.co/models/" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/models/</a>.</span></span></span>. <span id="S4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We utilize two text-to-image teacher models: Stable Diffusion v1-4 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al., 2022b</a>)</cite> and Midjourney <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Borji, 2022</a>)</cite>, along with the ModelScope text-to-video <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite> (1.7B parameters) and the SpeechT5 text-to-audio model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ao et al., 2022</a>)</cite> (144M parameters). For the text-to-image teacher models, we generate latent representations that are 32 <math id="S4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 32 dimensions (flattened to a 1024-dimensional vector) for each text input, using 20 diffusion inference steps and a guidance scale value of 7.5. Similar configurations apply for extracting latent representations from the text-to-video model, where 64 frames are generated for each text input. We extract the hidden representation from the first frame, resulting in a 512 <math id="S4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 512 hidden representation that is flattened into a 262144-dimensional vector for each text input. For the text-to-audio teacher model, we generate audio corresponding to each text input, which is subsequently processed by the Wav2Vec2-base model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Baevski et al., 2020</a>)</cite> to produce a 768-dimensional vector representation. These vector representations of the texts are utilized to pre-train the <span id="S4.p2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TS Aligner</span>. For natural language understanding (NLU) tasks, we employ cross-entropy loss for the pre-training of the <span id="S4.p2.1.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TS Aligner</span>. Conversely, for commonsense reasoning and instruction-tuning tasks, the <span id="S4.p2.1.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TS Aligner</span> is pre-trained using reconstruction loss measured by the mean squared error.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation metrics.</span> For CoLA and STS-B tasks, we use the Mathews correlation coefficient (‘Mcc’) and Pearson’s correlation coefficient (‘Pear’), respectively, for evaluation. For the remaining NLU and commonsense-reasoning tasks, we use the accuracy score (‘Acc’). For evaluating on instruction-tuning tasks, we use ‘RougeL’ metric.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span> The competing baselines include unimodal KD methods (KD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hinton et al., 2015</a>)</cite>, Sequence-KD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim and Rush, 2016</a>)</cite>, PKD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sun et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, TinyBERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiao et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, MetaDistil <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al., 2021</a>)</cite> and Rail KD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haidar et al., 2022</a>)</cite>) and multimodal KD methods (VL-BERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib90" title="" class="ltx_ref">Su et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, VisualBERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib91" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, ViLBERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib92" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al., 2019</a>)</cite>, Vokenization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib73" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tan and Bansal, 2020</a>)</cite>, VidLanKD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, Visual guidance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib79" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2021</a>)</cite> and X-adapter <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib93" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>). Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Baselines ‣ From Images to Words: Efficient Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation to Language Models from Black-box Teachers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a> presents more details.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S4.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:476.8pt;height:154.3pt;vertical-align:-75.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-102.2pt,33.1pt) scale(0.7,0.7) ;">
<table id="S4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Distillation type</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CoLA</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MRPC</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RTE</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">STS-B</span></th>
<th id="S4.T2.2.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T2.2.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CB</span></th>
